  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-15T16:05:18.061Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Would be ideal to offer some way to bind nearby bone chains together using different parameters. Rest distances can be calculated and cached for them, and then there should be parameters such as Togetherness or Cloth Pull to be able to control how much force is applied in order to hold bones together. As different parts of the chain move and are grabbed, it should apply spring forces in order to maintain the resting distance between the bones, and to both of the bones involved in the distance. This allows them to follow others when being grabbed and flow more naturally when colliding with limbs.",
